    "review_markdown": "Buying 300 EBL at Tk 26.6 (gross Tk 7,980, commission Tk 31.92, cash Tk 8,011.92) raises total market value from Tk 631,708.80 to Tk 639,838.80. EBL weight increases from 5.15% to 6.35%; Bank sector weight rises from 23.89% to 24.86% (target 25%). Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals weight falls from 37.78% to 37.3% (target 30%). SQURPHARMA weight falls from 25.44% to 25.12% (limit 25%). The trade matches three journal theses: adding to EBL at a low price against book value, and adding a cheap second bank to spread exposure beyond BRACBANK. No new rule violations are created; existing breaches (Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals above target, SQURPHARMA above limit) persist.\n\n- What the trade does to weights and rules: EBL weight rises to 6.35%, Bank sector weight to 24.86% (target 25%), Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals falls to 37.3% (target 30%), SQURPHARMA falls to 25.12% (limit 25%). [q:39182e5e-0403-4aa8-a4c9-554cee79f479]\n\n- Thesis check: the trade matches j-027 (adding to EBL at a low price against book value), j-018 (adding to EBL at a low price against book value) and j-006 (adding a cheap second bank beyond BRACBANK). All verdicts are matching. [q:57986307-f802-4e18-b182-e76e5cc32141]\n\n**What I remembered**\n- Week to 2026-09-17: no rule broken; EBL rose 6.2%, the largest move. [q:mem-54]\n\n**What to look at next**\n- SQURPHARMA's weight relative to its 25% limit\n- Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals weight relative to its 30% target\n\nNot covered: announcements between 2026-09-01 and 2026-10-01 for EBL\n\nYou asked what to trade. This review explains what happened; the decision stays with you.\n\nThis is a review of your own records, not financial advice.",
